      fixed_red(n)=2*C(n-2,3)+C(n-3,2)
   rectangle residues are local 4-cycles; hourglass residues link adjacent bridges.

READING
  The value 12 is a three-level alignment: R(4)=U(5)=SC(6)=12.  It is not the additive correction at the first shifted failure; that correction is 8, with R(5)=48 and U(6)=56.
  The clean recurrence object is not U(n) alone.  It is the transport ladder parent class + incident word orbit -> rooted child -> unrooted sink, with deletion fibers and edge-sector orientation as sidecars.
  Cross-sector orientation repairs the only size/internal edge-sector collision at U(6), a converse pair.  S217's rectangle/hourglass residues are the analogous repair coordinates for fixed-path diagonal flow.
  For LRC, the useful moral is: when a quotient produces a magical small integer, ask whether it is a class count, a rooted-perspective count, a self-converse fixed branch, an incident-word orbit count, a deletion-fiber multiplicity, or a cycle-space residue.
